ff' AND 'retry count'), and that a backoff-only fix would be incomplete. The builder replaced the entire parenthetical with the line-precise enumeration, so 'retry count' is gone and correctly superseded by 'ONE immediate unconditional retry (111)'. No further action needed.\n- [OK] **Concern B — criterion 5 is now genuinely re-derivable.** Commit 2bb21d4e (2026-08-08 07:33:55) adds 4 logs under logs/revalidation-2026-08-08/ plus a 3-file run-scoped invocation recipe. Criterion-5 dimensions all satisfied in the committed logs: B2 `backend_spawn_count=1 proxy_processes=2 persistent_proxies=1 reconnect_fired=False`, `B2_RESULT pass=True`; B2b same counts, `B2B_RESULT pass=True schema_validation_failures=2`.\n- [OK] **The run is provably GENUINE, not a copied baseline.** I pre-captured the baseline fingerprints, so a copy was detectable. Fresh vs baseline: epoch_ms 1786174296580 (07:31:36Z) vs 1786160919177 (03:48:39Z); PIDs [1802773, 1803369, be 1803407] vs [683845, 683886, be 683993]; B2 add(2,3) delta_ms **2504** vs committed 2373 vs #279 testimonial 1630 vs report.md n=3 1830/1814/1799 — a fourth distinct value. B2b: 1711/80/8/6 vs baseline 1695/119/9/7. Proxy log PIDs/epochs match its own harness log internally. The harness traceback cites the BUILDER's worktree path (pp3g-6l7c/.../intercept_poc.py:90) — real execution provenance.\n- [OK] **Verbatim ErrorResult preserved byte-for-byte.** I compared fresh vs baseline `message_verbatim` strings character by character (both the {'result': 5.0} and {'result': 2.0} instances): identical. session.py:1110 appears in the committed traceback — criterion 4 incidentally corroborated dynamically.\n- [OK] **Tracked baselines provably NOT modified.** Two independent proofs: (i) all four baseline blob hashes at 2bb21d4e match the values I captured before the commit existed — 48869ec2 / 13c04139 / 78f13293 / 6371dd22; (ii) `git diff 5bc6c993 2bb21d4e -- logs/n3/ tests/ report.md` is EMPTY. The commit is additive only (822 insertions, 0 deletions).\n- [OK] **Harness fidelity verified — the re-run used an equivalent harness.** This was the load-bearing risk in the copy-out approach. phase_b2_poc.py and phase_b2b_preabsorbed.py copies are BYTE-IDENTICAL to the tracked originals (empty diffs). common_c2.py differs ONLY in `LOGS_DIR = HERE / 'logs' / 'revalidation-2026-08-08'` plus an explanatory comment (4 insertions, 1 deletion). `HERE = parent.parent` resolves identically in both locations (both are direct children of c2-gap-investigation) — and the outcome proves it: logs landed exactly where that expression computes. Run-scoped subdirectories also match existing repo precedent (logs/n3/).\n\n### Process Assessment\n\n- [OK] Cadence healthy: positions at 07:27, 07:27, 07:33, 07:34, 07:34, handoff 07:35. Max gap ~6 min against a 10-15 min expected interval — never approached the 2x staleness threshold. **No trigger fired at any point.**\n- [OK] WZSE lesson honoured: commit landed 07:33:55, position posted 07:33 — artifacts and positions advanced in lockstep, no false staleness call.\n- [OK] PVi7 lesson honoured: liveness positively confirmed via the active #287 lock held by pp3g-6l7c before any assessment; no absence call was ever made.\n- [OK] AGENTS.md reasoning-certainty respected — builder supplied WHAT-NOT-TESTED clauses on both the result and the corrected-criterion comment (single-version point re-run; asserts at :104/:110 not exercised).\n- [OK] Playbook §5.9 / #271 satisfied: decision-gating artifacts are in git, not /tmp. Commit references gh#287.\n\n### Systemic Risks Identified\n\n- **Minor citation imprecision (non-blocking, cosmetic).** The #279 settle-note (07:34) says 'the committed logs (logs/phase-b2-*, logs/n3/) carry the ORIGINAL run numbers (1830/119/9/7)'. Strictly, 1830 belongs to logs/n3/phase-b2-poc-run1-harness.log; the top-level logs/phase-b2-poc-harness.log carries **2373** (report.md:474-477 explains this as a load-affected single run). 119/9/7 are exact. Impact: 